    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §61, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4800\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to authorizing farm distillery licensees to sell gift items\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To allow farm distilleries to sell\ngift items.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 2-c of section 61 of the alcoholic\nbeverage control law by adding a new paragraph (h) Section 2:\nEffective date\n\nJUSTIFICATION: For New York State's four farm-based beverage licenses,\nthree of which have provisions to explicitly allow for\nnon-manufactured items (marketing materials, gifts, apparel, etc.) to\nbe sold on premises However, farm distillers do not have such a\nprovision, thus making sales of other products sold at each distillery\na prohibited activity.\n\nFarm-based beverage producers, as tourism destinations and regional\ndraws, generate revenue through gifts and destination-specific items.\nThis bill would provide equity for farm distillers with the other\nfarm-based beverage licenses.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: new bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: none to state\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: this act shall take effect immediately\n\n",
